From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: mediatek,mtu3: add mediatek,force-vbus

The controller has an input for VBUS and a register that overrides it.
On boards where that input doesn't follow the cable, the controller stays
off the bus. Add a property for them.

The vendor tree of the MediaTek MT6897 has the same property.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml
@@ -201,6 +201,12 @@
             105 - used by mt8195, IP2, specific 1.05;
             106 - used by mt8195, IP3, specific 1.06;
           enum: [1, 2, 101, 102, 103, 105, 106]
+
+  mediatek,force-vbus:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      The controller can't sense VBUS on this board. Tell it that VBUS is
+      there whenever the device function is started.
 
   mediatek,u3p-dis-msk:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
